#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604616 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5459f0c-1eb6-5dba-828b-ab6a6f4e5a55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604432}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604432} :answer-field/id #uuid "47f7f112-87ba-552d-9bb8-3ac461686805" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604500} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68e83df2-aba5-55a1-8fc1-ef2c2a65026d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604324}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604324} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a882650-5a0d-5009-9b74-8d5dda92188f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604501} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbd6285b-9b3d-5b05-83b8-c709475213de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604439}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604439} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1e5ed5f-7786-5034-9ae9-c27a1bb0f473" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604527} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cac4d593-370a-5637-be73-4fba331c6e8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604423}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604423} :answer-field/id #uuid "f723ac45-173c-5f24-b300-04ee475710c3" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604559}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ce1947c5-ab86-5a81-ab9f-f80633f35f4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-317518" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6y &=18 \\\\ 5x &=-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-6$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td><td>\n</td><td>\n</td><td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>$=$</td>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-20$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $x$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ Similarly, the variable $y$ does not appear in the second equation, which means that its coefficient is $0$ too. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x-6y &=18 \\\\ 5x+0y &=-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}]}
